 "questions": [
  {
   "id": 493938,
   "is_answer_order_important": false,
   "stimulus_html": "",
   "stem_html": "Represent the set of all upper-case letters of the English alphabet using both the roster method and set builder notation.",
   "answers": [],
   "hints": [],
   "formats": [
    "free-response"
   ],
   "combo_choices": [],
   "collaborator_solutions": [
    {
     "images": [],
     "solution_type": "summary",
     "content_html": "<p>The roster method lists the individual members of the set inside curly braces, separated by commas. Once you have established the pattern, you can use the ellipsis to avoid needing to list them all. Be sure to list the final member of the set (Z) to avoid giving the appearance of an infinite set.</p>\n<p><span data-math=\"A = \\left\\{ {A,{\\rm{\\ }}B,{\\rm{\\ }}C,{\\rm{\\ }}D,{\\rm{ }} \\cdots ,{\\rm{\\ }}Z} \\right\\}\"></span></p>\n<p>Set builder notation uses a letter to represent a sample member of the set, a vertical bar, and then a description of a sample member.</p>\n<span data-math=\"A = \\left\\{ {a|a\\,\\,{\\rm{is\\ a\\ capital\\ letter\\ of\\ the\\ English\\ alphabet}}} \\right\\}\"></span>"
    },
    {
     "images": [],
     "solution_type": "detailed",
     "content_html": "<p>Roster method: <span data-math=\"\\{ \\text{A, B, C, } \\ldots \\text{, Z}\\},\">\\{ \\text{A,B,C,} \\ldots \\text{,Z}\\},</span> and set builder notation: <span data-math=\"\\{ x|x{\\text{ is a capital letter of the English alphabet}}\\}\">\\{ x|x{\\text{is a capital letter of the English alphabet}}\\}</span></p>"
    }
   ],
   "community_solutions": []
  }
 ],
